    ex("py-07", "Retry decorator", "Functions & Decorators", A,
       "Write a decorator factory `retry(times)` that calls the wrapped function up to `times` times, retrying only when it raises an exception, and re-raises the last exception if all attempts fail. Use functools.wraps.",
       ["A decorator factory returns a decorator which returns a wrapper.", "Track the last exception and raise it after the loop."],
       "import functools\n\ndef retry(times):\n    pass\n",
       "A function failing twice then succeeding returns normally with retry(3).",
       "import functools\n\ndef retry(times):\n    def deco(fn):\n        @functools.wraps(fn)\n        def wrapper(*a, **k):\n            last = None\n            for _ in range(times):\n                try:\n                    return fn(*a, **k)\n                except Exception as e:\n                    last = e\n            raise last\n        return wrapper\n    return deco\n",
       "calls = {'n': 0}\n@retry(3)\ndef flaky():\n    calls['n'] += 1\n    if calls['n'] < 3:\n        raise ValueError('boom')\n    return 'ok'\nassert flaky() == 'ok' and calls['n'] == 3\n\n@retry(2)\ndef always():\n    raise KeyError('x')\ntry:\n    always()\n    assert False, 'should raise'\nexcept KeyError:\n    pass\nassert flaky.__name__ == 'flaky'",
       "Retries are a core pipeline resilience pattern; production versions add exponential backoff and only retry transient errors."),
